# Build output and caches only. Nothing here may exclude first-party source:
# analyzers/gitignore_check.py will flag this file if it ever does, and running
# Chronicle on Chronicle is part of the submission (spec §10, hours 44-48).

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.venv/
venv/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local HACKPROOF state: a roster and the enrollment cards it is built from carry
# participants' public keys and email addresses, which is personal data under the
# retention policy in spec §11. Keep them out of git and delete them after judging.
#
# These must cover every path analyzers/gpg_check.py:ROSTER_CANDIDATES actually
# looks in, or the default location is the one that leaks. `*.roster.json` alone
# did not: the candidate filenames are `hackproof-roster.json` and
# `chronicle-roster.json`, which end in `-roster.json`, not `.roster.json`.
.hackproof/
.chronicle/
roster.json
*-roster.json
*.roster.json
enrollment-*.json
